{"_id":"codex:chapter:23:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Simulation and Reality","seq":123,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","simulation","reality"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 23"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:23:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Simulation and Reality","seq":123,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Simulation allows us to test futures, but it is not reality. Reality is accountable to evidence and consequence. Simulation must be labelled, isolated, and governed by policies that prevent leakage into operational truth. The Codex mandates: (1) clear differentiation between simulated and real data, (2) rollback paths for projections tested in simulation, (3) prohibition of governance by simulation results alone without empirical validation. Simulation is a tool for reflection, not a substitute for the world."}
